    "lawCode": "Add §§1202-oo & 1202-pp, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8155\n\nSPONSOR: GRIFFO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to authorizing occupancy taxes\nin the city of Utica and the city of Rome; and providing for the repeal\nof such provisions upon the expiration thereof\n\nThe Cities of Utica and Rome have requested this legislation as the\nadditional revenue generated from the hotel/motel occupancy tax will\nenable both cities to attract new travel and tourism business and\nincrease visitation, which in turn will retain and create jobs to keep\nthe economic impact of travel working to benefit Oneida County and the\ngreater Mohawk Valley.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2025- New Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nLOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nIncreased revenue for the Cities of Utica and Rome.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
